# taurine.msf
# 2-Aminoethanesulfonic acid (taurine)
# pKa1=1.500 (sulfonic acid SO3H → SO3-), pKa2=9.060 (NH3+ → NH2)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Sulfonic acid pKa1 is new FG (lower than carboxylate by ~2 units).
# Zwitterionic amino-sulfonate covers the physiological pH 7-9 gap.

